Subject: String append in place when the one count is the local slot that takes the result back

What this does
  - Compiled `s += x` whose left operand comes from `get_local S` (the old value used nowhere else, no window or edge copy) and whose result goes only to `put_local S` is emitted with a flag (0x100 in the sub argument of qjs_aot_binary_rr).
  - regvm_accum_append_u takes a new argument own1: with it a string of count one is extended in place (or regrown), as the slot is the one holder and gets the same pointer back.

Why we need it
  pdfjs builds strings in variables (Type1Parser eexecStr += ...). The string is owned by the slot, so the in-place test (count 0 and parked) failed every time and each append copied the whole string. pdfjs AOT 7759 -> 10312.

Soundness
  Count one with the slot as the only user of the old value and of the new one: no other holder can see the longer string. Register and argument aliases are still scanned. QJS_AOT_NOVARAPP=1 in the generator turns the flag off.

